1
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,720
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,720
Episode 13

3
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,120
Boatman! A little further in, please.

4
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:29,040
Boatman,
please take us a little farther in.

5
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,200
Get out.

6
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,720
Weren't you training recruits?
What brings you here?

7
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,600
I missed Yan, so here I am.

8
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,240
Come aboard.

9
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,560
Sixty-three.

10
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,240
-Can he really…
-Here.

11
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,960
Hiding in his courtyard,
out of the wind and rain…

12
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:11,360
He's a weakling!

13
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,320
Look. He really can do it!

14
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,800
He's got some skill.

15
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,080
Who'd have thought?

16
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,520
Tie another knot.

17
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:33,880
He really knows how!

18
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,200
What do we do?

19
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,800
-Has he measured it?
-Still measuring. Looks good.

20
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:38,880
Keep looking.

21
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,960
You make everything worse!

22
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,600
Useless, all of you!

23
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:50,360
What have I always taught you?

24
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,440
Lord Lu.

25
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,760
Thank you. Thank you.

26
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:02,720
River survey report
Revised: Navigable

27
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,440
There are no obstructions here.

28
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,000
The ships can pass.

29
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,080
Now that spring's here,
our Grain Transport Office

30
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,200
is at its busiest.

31
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,760
I never expected such a mistake.

32
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,680
It wasn't a mistake.

33
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,080
Someone did it on purpose.

34
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,720
I've been staying at the docks,

35
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,400
and found officials

36
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,440
falsifying depth reports to line
their pockets.

37
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,800
Under imperial law,

38
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,280
river officials and laborers

39
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,840
who falsify depth reports

40
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,560
and delay the grain ships

41
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:35,360
receive 100 strokes
and three years' imprisonment.

42
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:37,120
If it harms the affairs of state,

43
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,240
the punishment increases.

44
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,520
You're a fair, honest man, Lord Lu,

45
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,840
who cares for the people.

46
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,520
Today,

47
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,880
our family's grievance is a small thing.

48
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,040
But violating imperial law,

49
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,800
and harming countless people
along this river is not.

50
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,960
Please, Lord Lu,

51
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,240
give our family,

52
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,720
and all the people along this river,

53
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,800
justice.

54
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,440
Everyone here can bear witness!

55
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,480
-Yes!
-Give us justice!

56
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:06,320
Give us justice!

57
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,040
Rest assured.

58
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,200
Give us justice!

59
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:14,080
I will get to the bottom of this.

60
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,840
Find out the whole truth.

61
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,000
There will be no leniency!

62
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,440
You can all rest easy.

63
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:22,240
Good! Good! Good!

64
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,840
Have you found out?

65
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,000
An honored guest from the capital

66
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,560
specifically ordered a thorough survey.

67
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,520
Good intentions gone wrong.

68
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:41,920
That honored guest is very thoughtful.

69
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,800
I've had bad luck lately.

70
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,640
Obstacles at every turn.

71
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,680
Baozhu had a fright, too.

72
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,000
Some ill-wisher must be behind it.

73
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,400
We need an exorcism at once,

74
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,480
or the whole clan could suffer.

75
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,720
Careful.

76
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,200
Let him through.

77
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,920
I've been angry lately, too.

78
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,440
Master, take a good look.

79
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,400
See what you can find.

80
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,720
Don't worry, Mother.

81
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,800
Here.

82
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,400
What… what are the Xies doing?

83
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:45,400
My grandson got hurt saving one of you!

84
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,680
He's still in bed!

85
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,040
Poor boy!

86
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,840
So they drove you here.

87
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:03,560
I was wondering
why they were being so kind.

88
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,840
It's cold.

89
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,760
Get me some hot water.

90
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,480
Yingtao! Yingtao!

91
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,440
Go! Go!

92
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,360
What's that smell?

93
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,920
Fire!

94
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,760
Fire!

95
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,240
Fire!

96
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,640
Fire!

97
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,920
Help! Fire!

98
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,320
Fire!

99
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,920
Open the door! Fire!

100
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:09,880
Fire!

101
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,200
Fire!

102
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,280
Don't injuries take 100 days to heal?

103
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,920
Things have been so unsettled here lately.

104
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,040
You've come at a bad time.

105
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,840
You're all better now, aren't you?

106
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,640
Why not return to the capital early,

107
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:57,440
before the bad luck rubs off on you?

108
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,040
But…

109
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:03,840
We've come all this way in all sincerity.

110
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:07,360
Our families are old friends.

111
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:10,840
You're welcome to visit.

112
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,480
But

113
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:16,800
a marriage between us
is out of the question.

114
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:21,920
The young people
weren't meant for each other,

115
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,560
were they?

116
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:29,800
Matron Fang, help me to my room.

117
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:34,440
I'm rather tired.

118
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,000
Please send someone tomorrow

119
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,480
to register the cancellation
at the Yangzhou county office.

120
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,400
Let's settle this soon,

121
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,600
before we get in the way
of your family's bright future.

122
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,280
Let's go.

123
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,680
Yi, stop acting.

124
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,480
Mother, how did you know it was me?

125
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,760
But please don't scold me.

126
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,880
Hungry?

127
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,840
I'll have the kitchen make you something.

128
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:48,960
Yes, Mother!

129
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,280
I'm starving!

130
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:53,560
What was that? Look at all these dust!

131
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:58,680
Let's go, Grandmother.

132
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,400
The paperwork's ready.

133
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,680
You've disgraced us!

134
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,920
This isn't over!

135
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,320
When we get back,
Father can report them to the court!

136
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,680
Idiot!

137
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:10,560
Xie Yan is Ye Xianggao's grandson!

138
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,120
Your father still depends on him!

139
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,680
We can act in secret,

140
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:15,760
but who'd dare move openly?

141
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,480
Where's Youqing?

142
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,440
Wasn't she told to wait in the carriage?

143
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,360
Where's Miss Huang?

144
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,160
Madam, sir, she left this letter.

145
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,120
<i>My sword's gone.</i>

146
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,200
<i>I'll have another forged.</i>

147
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,480
<i>Don't worry about me.</i>

148
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,680
This…

149
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,080
This…

150
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,720
The Xie estate

151
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,160
How did it go?

152
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,080
As you instructed,

153
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,840
I went to the Shen courtyard

154
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,280
and asked if

155
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,280
Mr. Huang had been misdiagnosed.

156
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,520
Lady Shen said

157
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,880
that lately, Mr. Song had been distracted.

158
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,040
That's why he was careless.

159
00:10:57,760 --> 00:11:00,800
She punished him severely on the spot.

160
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,400
Jingxing is a good boy.

161
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:06,000
What a pity.

162
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,520
There's something I don't understand.

163
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:12,080
If he's so good,

164
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,360
Madam,

165
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,520
why not do him a favor

166
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,760
and recommend him for office?

167
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,680
He could be another ally for us.

168
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:24,280
That's why I kept him in this family.

169
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:29,480
But I had someone look into his
background.

170
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,480
It's strange.

171
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,480
Both parents died in one night,

172
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:39,160
and he came all the way to Yangzhou alone.

173
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,400
Really?

174
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,920
It's not that I distrust him.

175
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:48,520
But we must be careful.

176
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,920
Over the years,

177
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,280
he's done a great deal for us.

178
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:57,360
Give him a little more private allowance.

179
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:00,520
He can open a clinic or a business.

180
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,640
Just don't let him keep asking me

181
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,240
for that letter of recommendation.

182
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,160
Yes.

183
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:13,040
And go to the storeroom

184
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,360
and find some good satin

185
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,920
and send it to Baozhu.

186
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:20,000
A little gift from me.

187
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,120
Tell her not to worry.

188
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,080
Yes.

189
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:27,800
And make sure the colors are bright.

190
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,600
Yes.

191
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,840
The new steward and accountant
seem dependable.

192
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,560
The various offices
have sent us a total of

193
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:38,760
3,200 dan of grain.

194
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,080
Baozhu!

195
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:46,920
You're home.

196
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,800
Do you like the satin?

197
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,400
My legs hurt.

198
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,600
Will you take a look?

199
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:20,760
My legs hurt.

200
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,640
Take a look.

201
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:26,960
They look pretty nimble to me.

202
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:30,080
I rushed back to speak up for you!

203
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:31,280
It was all for you!

204
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,360
And not a kind word!

205
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,080
For me?

206
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:36,920
Did I invite the Huangs here?

207
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:40,000
You caused all of this,
and I had to deal with it!

208
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:41,280
Where were you?

209
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:42,480
Nowhere to be seen!

210
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,960
Now you swoop in to save me.
What am I supposed to say?

211
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,880
Well done! Well done!

212
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,760
I wasn't having much fun either.

213
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,520
I rode back as fast as I could.

214
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,320
My legs are rubbed raw!
Did I tell you that?

215
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,440
I only want what's best for you.

216
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:58,480
And this is how you treat me?

217
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,520
You're the eldest legitimate Xie son.

218
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,040
Everyone cares if your legs hurt.

219
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,280
What about me?

220
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,800
Bandits attacked, and no one cared.

221
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:08,280
I said a few sharp words, and got slapped!

222
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,000
Twice!

223
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,040
Who?

224
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,760
I'll chop his hands off!

225
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,040
Your grandmother.

226
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,160
Are you all right?

227
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,680
I don't need your concern!

228
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,640
Think of it as slapping me twice.

229
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,960
I'll demand justice tomorrow morning.

230
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:38,680
She's already sent an apology.
Why make more fuss?

231
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:39,840
What do you want, then?

232
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,160
I want shops.

233
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:42,640
I want a family rank.

234
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,120
I want to earn my own money.

235
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,920
Anything but that.
I'll give you anything else.

236
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,360
Fine. Then make sure no one dares slap me,

237
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,360
looks down on me,
or punishes me on a whim!

238
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,440
Can you give me that?

239
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,080
How about this?

240
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,600
Give me a year.

241
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,960
I'll take charge of
the family's most important route.

242
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,040
-Then I'll protect you.
-I don't want you!

243
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,360
Why can't you understand?

244
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:10,920
You don't want me?

245
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,120
Don't stand there looking pitiful!

246
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,800
Now that your legs are better,
you get to go and enjoy yourself,

247
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,040
while I have to stay here
running around fixing your problems!

248
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,640
I have my own things to do!

249
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,520
You know so little,
and want to run a shop?

250
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,880
With your temper,

251
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,400
you'll get into trouble
without someone watching you!

252
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,720
No!

253
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,640
If you're afraid of choking,
you might as well stop eating!

254
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,840
I'm doing this for your own good!
Why can't you understand?

255
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,720
I just want to shelter you
from wind and rain.

256
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,040
No!

257
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,320
I'll command the wind and rain myself!

258
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,040
She's let it go to her head,

259
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:01,040
humiliating the Huangs in public!

260
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:06,760
Madam couldn't be more biased!

261
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,520
That punishment was just for show!

262
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:12,760
I say she wasn't hit hard enough!

263
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,560
She hasn't learned!

264
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,000
You hate her most of all.

265
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,480
Why so quiet?

266
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,040
Sticky rice glued your mouth shut?

267
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,720
You talk too much.

268
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,240
What?

269
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:48,200
Don't you like any of these?

270
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:49,840
Your…

271
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:51,480
your face!

272
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:55,760
Was it because
I exposed the Huangs that you…

273
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,040
No.

274
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,400
Besides, you didn't ask
the Huangs to come here.

275
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:04,040
I heard what happened.

276
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:09,320
And this medicine

277
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:11,200
reduces swelling and bruising.

278
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,160
-Here.
-No need.

279
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,640
This is nothing.

280
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:15,800
Keep it for yourself.

281
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:18,320
Take it.

282
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:20,240
I'll feel better knowing you have it.

283
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,640
Thank you.

284
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,080
They beat my legs with a rod.

285
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,800
It's hard to stand.

286
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,840
You should get well soon

287
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,160
and open your clinic.

288
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,640
Stop letting people here bully you.

289
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,480
What about you?

290
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,640
Me?

291
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,640
I don't know.

292
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:12,920
Afraid you'll throw too hard

293
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,400
and frighten the little fish?

294
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,520
You're too softhearted.

295
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,680
They're trapped here. That's sad enough.

296
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,840
How could I be so cruel?

297
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,280
Don't think of it like that.

298
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,320
Here, at least they get fed.

299
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,760
Anywhere else,

300
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:27,840
they'd be caught

301
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,920
and made into fish soup.

302
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,720
Trapped in this tiny space,

303
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,120
at someone else's mercy…

304
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,040
Is food all that matters?

305
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:39,440
Why not find a way out together,

306
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,920
instead of begging for scraps?

307
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,000
Good idea!

308
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:51,400
You've helped me realize something.

309
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:53,600
People thrive when they move on.

310
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,400
I'd better find another way.

311
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,520
Thank you!

312
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:19,480
My lord, last year's account books.

313
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,840
My lord, the books from the year before.

314
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,120
This year's books are with Lady Jin.

315
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,840
What does she want them for?

316
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,760
She wants to learn.

317
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,320
Says they may come in handy someday.

318
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,880
I just saw her go out.

319
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:52,800
If you want the books,

320
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,480
you may have to wait.

321
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,200
My lord...

322
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,280
Look.

323
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,040
What does that look like?

324
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,840
Like what?

325
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:10,080
Doesn't it look like
the word for "prisoner"?

326
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:12,560
"Prisoner"…

327
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:25,920
You've come to demand justice?

328
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,080
Yes.

329
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,520
I know you've been wronged.

330
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,840
The Huangs were at fault,

331
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,560
but you were out of line, too.

332
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:39,760
Luckily, Yan's grandfather
is an official in the capital.

333
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:43,520
What if the tables turn someday,

334
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,360
and they rise to power,

335
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,240
still bearing a grudge?

336
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,560
What then?

337
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:52,720
I had Matron Fang punish you

338
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,960
because I had no choice.

339
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:58,000
I understand. I accept what you say.

340
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:00,760
I lost my temper and offended our guests.

341
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:02,640
But I still

342
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:04,520
can't swallow it.

343
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,520
Since I came here,

344
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:10,160
I've done my best
for the Xies and Xie Yan.

345
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,120
Yet I was humiliated in public.

346
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,440
You brushed it aside to save face.

347
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:16,240
Is that fair?

348
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:27,360
Gold, jewels, silk, satin…

349
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,880
Have we ever denied you anything?

350
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:35,560
I chose that rose-pink fabric
for you myself.

351
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,160
Go and ask around.

352
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,200
In a family like ours,

353
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:47,040
for a concubine to be treated like this
is a great honor!

354
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:48,840
That's very nice,

355
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:51,160
but it's not what I want.

356
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:53,880
You don't even want honor?

357
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:59,080
I used to haggle for a few more coins,

358
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,360
arguing till I was red in the face.

359
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:01,760
No dignity at all.

360
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:03,680
But I was happy,

361
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:05,240
because I earned money.

362
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,200
Now I've cast the divination blocks,

363
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,760
put on red, and gained some dignity.

364
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,360
But I'm not happy.

365
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,000
I didn't know why.

366
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,680
Then I realized.

367
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:19,120
I've got nothing of my own.

368
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:21,800
The rewards aren't enough?

369
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:24,520
You've come for more?

370
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:26,560
I help your grandson, Xie Yan,

371
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,320
make his way in the world
and build his future.

372
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,720
What about me?

373
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:33,720
I can't spend my whole life
running around after him.

374
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:37,560
You live in luxury,

375
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:38,880
and you're still not satisfied?

376
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:41,240
So do you.

377
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,240
Are you satisfied?

378
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,400
How dare you!

379
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:48,560
I'm not satisfied.

380
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:49,880
Call me greedy.

381
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:52,640
I've come to ask for my own way forward.

382
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,200
What exactly do you want?

383
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,400
Let me take over Xi's position

384
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:58,600
and run the shops.

385
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,640
How much can you read now?

386
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,160
Most of it.

387
00:23:05,240 --> 00:23:07,160
If I can't read something,
I can look it up,

388
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,320
or ask someone.

389
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:09,960
I'm quick with numbers,

390
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,760
healthy, and not afraid of hard work.

391
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,600
All right.

392
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:21,560
I'll give you the shops.

393
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,280
If you do well,

394
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:25,200
you'll get a rank.

395
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:27,320
Thank you, Madam!

396
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:29,560
May you live a hundred years,

397
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:30,680
with endless blessings!

398
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,640
I'll look forward to good news, then.

399
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:46,480
Even "look forward to good news"!

400
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,800
A born scholar!

401
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:52,000
Come out.

402
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,320
Why did you come to see me?

403
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:01,960
Why hide

404
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:03,280
when there's nothing wrong?

405
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:05,680
About the same thing.

406
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,800
To ask me to take back my promise?

407
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:12,600
No.

408
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,200
Please give it to her.

409
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,120
Thank you, Grandmother.

410
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:29,840
Look at that long face!

411
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,120
Regret it now?

412
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:33,720
You did their dirty work,

413
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,640
got nothing for it,

414
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:37,720
and took a beating!

415
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:42,720
Who's with you?

416
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,640
Clear now?

417
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:56,200
Poor little young master!

418
00:24:57,400 --> 00:25:00,040
Betraying us, and no one wants you.

419
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:05,160
In the end, I have to pick you up again.

420
00:25:09,720 --> 00:25:11,520
My lady, the lady of the house is here.

421
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,000
Your daughter-in-law wants to practice,

422
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:22,600
so why come asking for my shops?

423
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:28,000
When the master came home,

424
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:30,200
he took half your husband's routes.

425
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,280
There was some bad feeling.

426
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,440
Then Yan had all that trouble.

427
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:39,760
So the shops were put in your care.

428
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,880
He's better now.

429
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:45,000
Please return them to their owner.

430
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,160
Listen to you!

431
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:49,880
What?

432
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:51,920
As if we owed you something!

433
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,320
You couldn't keep them going,

434
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:56,000
and begged us to take them!

435
00:25:56,080 --> 00:25:57,560
Now they're doing well,

436
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:58,920
you want them back?

437
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,800
Are we dogs to be led about
whenever you please?

438
00:26:02,760 --> 00:26:03,760
Besides,

439
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:06,520
I've worked so hard just to break even!

440
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,120
Who does she think she is?

441
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:09,240
Can she manage?

442
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:10,880
If she loses money,

443
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,440
who takes responsibility?

444
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:13,560
You?

445
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:17,760
I'm not here to force your hand.

446
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:20,920
Just to explain what's at stake.

447
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:22,920
You decide.

448
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:30,520
Fine.

449
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:34,520
Let's hear what you have to say.

450
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:37,560
While you've run the shops,

451
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:39,720
half the monthly profits

452
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:42,520
go to household expenses.

453
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:46,720
By rights, a fifth of what's left

454
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:48,880
should go to Yan's private allowance.

455
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:53,200
I've only just
taken charge of the household,

456
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:57,360
and discovered that never happened.

457
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,520
That's the first point.

458
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:04,520
Second, all those concerns of yours

459
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:07,200
have already occurred to Madam.

460
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:08,840
We've discussed it with her.

461
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:11,920
You've run these shops for so long,

462
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,760
you know them better than we do.

463
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:17,000
Too many would be beyond us.

464
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:22,200
So we only want the salt shop back.

465
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:26,680
Keep the rest for your trouble.

466
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:36,640
I can't decide this.

467
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,800
I'll have to speak to my husband.

468
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:43,800
This is outrageous!

469
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:47,120
They didn't want the child.

470
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:49,200
We worked hard to raise it,

471
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:50,760
and now they want it back!

472
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:52,560
Lady of the house?

473
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,240
Worse than a slave trader!

474
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:56,280
At least she came smiling.

475
00:27:56,560 --> 00:27:57,880
That's something.

476
00:27:58,240 --> 00:28:00,200
I hate the ones who plot in secret.

477
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:03,120
Want things, but won't say so!

478
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:07,360
Give up money that's already mine?

479
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:09,480
You might as well take my life!

480
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:11,840
What does my pride matter anyway?

481
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:14,640
Don't talk like that!

482
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:16,320
Money can be earned again.

483
00:28:16,720 --> 00:28:19,400
A life lost is lost for good.

484
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:24,520
You're right, my lady.

485
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:29,280
Money lost can be earned again.

486
00:28:29,360 --> 00:28:33,000
A shop given away can be taken back!

487
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:36,280
Look. Feel.

488
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:39,200
Enough, enough.

489
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:42,120
You really hit me!

490
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:45,760
Xie Salt Shop

491
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,400
Wipe that drool off.

492
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:51,880
Mind your own business.

493
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:55,120
Yours is here.

494
00:28:56,160 --> 00:28:57,360
Quite a send-off!

495
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:00,440
Come again!

496
00:29:02,360 --> 00:29:04,480
Isn't it only the government
that can sell salt?

497
00:29:05,560 --> 00:29:06,800
The state oversees it. Merchants sell.

498
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:08,840
Salt is a monopoly,

499
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:10,640
but the court doesn't sell it all itself.

500
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,280
It issues salt permits

501
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:14,440
to qualified merchants,
who sell it themselves.

502
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:17,000
Our ancestors served the court
through grain transport.

503
00:29:17,360 --> 00:29:18,880
That's how we got permission.

504
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:21,480
I'm talking to you!
Where are you going now?

505
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:23,680
Jin Baozhu!

506
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:27,200
At last!
You've kept your uncle and me waiting.

507
00:29:27,280 --> 00:29:28,360
Uncle, Aunt Shen.

508
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:32,440
This shop is yours to run now.

509
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,160
As your uncle,

510
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:36,720
I've a few things to explain.

511
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,120
Come, come, come. Over here.

512
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:41,680
Look. The salt on these shelves

513
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:43,240
was collected with my salt permits

514
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:45,400
from the Lianghuai saltworks.

515
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:49,840
The salt bears our family's own seals.

516
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:51,600
Each seal gives

517
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:53,880
the weight and place of origin,

518
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,760
and the salt permit number.

519
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:57,840
Check it against

520
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,160
the accountant's salt-permit register.

521
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:00,520
Understand?

522
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:03,280
And before closing each day,

523
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:04,560
you, as manager,

524
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:06,080
must check everything.

525
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:08,200
Seals, weights, numbers.

526
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:11,480
There must be no mistakes.

527
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,560
Manyun,

528
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:14,960
our niece is a clever girl.

529
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:16,160
She catches on quickly.

530
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:18,000
She'll do very well.

531
00:30:18,080 --> 00:30:19,080
Of course.

532
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:22,360
The manager, accountant, assistants…

533
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:24,640
You know what each of them does,

534
00:30:24,720 --> 00:30:26,400
so I won't go on.

535
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:30,040
But this salt shop
has a few rules of its own.

536
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:31,880
Using the official scales,

537
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:33,440
sealing the sacks, calling out entries…

538
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:35,640
Little things, really.

539
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:39,240
I've had the accountant
write down the procedures.

540
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:46,160
Later, my nephew can read them to you.

541
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:48,040
From now on,

542
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:50,640
this shop is yours to look after.

543
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,400
We'll go, then.

544
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:53,800
Let's go. Let's go.

545
00:30:53,960 --> 00:30:54,960
Take care.

546
00:30:58,120 --> 00:31:00,200
My lady, let's go home early.

547
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,280
So helpful? They must want something.

548
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:06,920
What do you think?

549
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:09,840
Jin Baozhu!

550
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,400
Jin--

551
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:13,960
Jin Baozhu!

552
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:16,480
I'm talking to you!
Are you listening, Jin Baozhu?

553
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:20,280
Remember,

554
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:22,880
everyone here has their own job,
and keeps an eye on the others.

555
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,800
Each night,
you must check the accounts carefully.

556
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,080
Are you listening?

557
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,800
Remember, peanuts and dried tofu together

558
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:29,920
taste like ham.

559
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:32,320
Why are you telling me that?

560
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:33,680
Why are you telling me all that?

561
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:35,320
I have my own ideas.
